3. Architecture Strategy — Today vs Future
Today: Modular monolith. One Node.js server, split into self-contained modules (routes, controller, service, repository, validation, events).
Future: If a service needs to scale, extract that module into a microservice. Modules must therefore stay loosely coupled.
Module rule: a module may call another module only through its service or through events. Never import another module's repository.
4. Golden Rules (apply to all code)
Readable • Maintainable • Scalable • Flexible • Modular • Reusable • Testable • Performant • Secure • Configurable • Loosely Coupled • Well Architected
No hardcoding. No hardcoded mapping. Values come from config, env, or the shared package.
Dynamic functionality wherever possible (config/DB driven, not if/else chains).
Enums, validation schemas and socket event names live in shared/ or config files only.
Dates: stored in ISO / UTC in DB; shown in the user's timezone on the frontend.
