11. Data Handling Rules
React Query: once data is fetched, do not call the API again when switching pages (use staleTime/cache). Invalidate only on change.
WebSocket: server sends "something changed" events; client invalidates matching query keys. Do not push full data.
Optimistic updates for single and bulk record updates; version column for conflict detection.
Bulk operations supported.
Version history for log records.
Time: UTC ISO in DB → user timezone in UI.
12. Offline & Network
Service worker (Workbox): app shell caching; support for import/export.
IndexedDB for offline data (no cookies).
Offline mode is read-only: dashboard and selected pages load; page refresh works offline; writes are blocked with a clear message.
Slow network detection: below 3G / response over 2000 ms shows an indicator icon. In slow/offline state users can view data but cannot update it.
13. API Design
Versioned: /api/v1.
Standard success/error response format.
Central error handling with error codes (from shared/).
Swagger documentation for the whole API.
14. Database (MySQL)
Migrations + seeds (default roles, permissions, app groups, admin user). Naming rules and ERD in docs/database/. All timestamps in UTC. version column on updatable records.
